Station: Kenpoly-convocation-arena, Bori Metropolis.

The vertical electrical sounding (VES) data identifies a five-layer subsurface model. The resistivity values follow a sequence of 1434 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, 1879 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, 318 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, 3488 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$, and 542 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$. Based on the specified notation for consecutive layer triplets, the sequence produces the following pattern: the first triplet (1434-1879-318) is K; the second (1879-318-3488) is H; and the third (318-3488-542) is K. Consequently, the calculated curve type is KHK. This result is consistent with the survey classification currently on file for this station.

